 """The post-quantum key-hash soft fork (OP_CHECKPQSIGVERIFY, src/script/pq.h) on regtest, end to end.
 
-Activates DEPLOYMENT_PQSIG through version bits, pays into a P2SH output whose redeem script is
-<pqkh> OP_CHECKPQSIGVERIFY using the ordinary wallet, then spends it with a transaction built and signed here
-in Python (dilithium-py, pure Python ML-DSA-44) so that the node is the only thing under test. Then the
-mutations a node must refuse, and the policy limit on the scriptSig size.
+Pays into a P2SH output whose redeem script is <pqkh> OP_CHECKPQSIGVERIFY with the ordinary wallet, then spends
+it with a transaction built and signed here in Python (dilithium-py, pure Python ML-DSA-44), so the node is the
+only thing under test. Shows the soft-fork property directly: before the activation height a block carrying a
+spend with a BAD signature is accepted (the opcode is a no-op to the old rules), after it the same block is
+rejected. Then the mutations a node must refuse, and the policy limit on the scriptSig size.
 """
 
